<title>INDIA: India TISCO 96/97 1st half net up 25 pct.</title>
<headline>India TISCO 96/97 1st half net up 25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	  2,522.2     vs	2,013.3</p>
<p>    Net sales	  30,212.9     vs     24,960.7</p>
<p>    Tax		     373.5     vs	Nil</p>
<p>    Other income	  379.8     vs	  172.3</p>
<p>    Interest	    1,669.9     vs	1,385.3</p>
<p>    Expenditure	23,986.3     vs     19,878.7</p>
<p>    Gross profit	4,936.5     vs	3,869.0</p>
<p>    Depreciation	1,621.1     vs	1,568.6</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit    2,895.7     vs	2,013.3</p>
<p>Note: Tata Iron and Steel Company Ltd (TISCO) said steel sales rose 8 percent, in which sale of hot rolled coils rose to 436,000 tonnnes in the first half from 282,000 tonnes in the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>Cement sales were higher at 629,300 tonnes against 443,200 tonnes. The pre-tax profit was arrived at after providing for exceptional items of 419.7 million rupees (for voluntary retirement compensation) against 287.1 million (including 170 million for energy optimising furnace) in year ago period.</p>
<p>--Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
